WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.470
- But since your show is
called "Never Have I Ever",

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.900
I think that we need to play
a quick round of "Never Ever"-

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.733
You've never played "Never Have I Ever".

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:07.150
- I've never done this in an interview.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:07.983
- Yeah, so we're gonna-
- No. This is so...

00:00:07.983 --> 00:00:09.850
for brand new first
time ever in your life,

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.489
we're gonna play "Never Have I Ever".

00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:14.817
♪ Never have I ever ♪

00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:15.700
(audience clapping)

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.020
All right. So grab your paddle.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:17.853
Here we go.

00:00:17.853 --> 00:00:19.970
I'm gonna hit this
button that's super close

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.090
in proximity to me.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.560
And we both have to
honestly say if we have

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.480
or we have never done whatever comes up.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.770
Are you ready?
- Okay.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.603
As I'll ever be.

00:00:29.603 --> 00:00:30.515
- All right. Here we go.

00:00:30.515 --> 00:00:32.013
- Boom.
- Boom.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.930
- [Maitreyi] Oh. This
is wow. This is like...

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:36.993
Gone skinny-dipping.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.420
'Cause I can't swim.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.334
So why would I want to be naked and drown?

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.485
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:42.485 --> 00:00:43.587
I can't swim!

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:46.027
I know like I need to work on that.

00:00:46.027 --> 00:00:47.610
I need to work on that. I know.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.302
I'm well aware.

00:00:49.302 --> 00:00:50.830
This is like a survival thing.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.774
But it's just like a lot of body movement.

00:00:52.774 --> 00:00:55.349
- You said, "Why would I ever
want to be naked and drown."

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:56.182
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:57.809
- I don't wanna be naked and drown.

00:00:57.809 --> 00:00:59.339
Like, I'm already gonna drown.

00:00:59.339 --> 00:01:01.190
Why would I wanna be naked while doing it?

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.960
- Oh, well, girl...

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.211
I grew up in the country.

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:06.086
(both laughing)

00:01:06.086 --> 00:01:07.130
So I definitely have.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:07.963
- Best response.

00:01:07.963 --> 00:01:09.230
- I'm just saying.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.830
I will tell you, I was terrified though

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.100
'cause I was also a nerd

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.800
and I loved like all the
history channel things

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.750
or Nat Geo or all that kind
of stuff when I was a kid.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.890
And I learned about this thing.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.620
Now, granted I think it was in the Amazon.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.920
But this little thing that can crawl

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.462
into like your lady bits

00:01:22.462 --> 00:01:24.840
and it can do some damage.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.510
And so I was kind of
afraid to be naked in water

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.230
even though I wasn't in the Amazon.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.950
I was like, "It's gonna get me!"

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.870
So I kinda swam like a mermaid.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.870
I was like, nothing's getting in there.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.694
- Nice. Protected.

00:01:36.694 --> 00:01:37.690
(both laughing)

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.070
- I was protecting my goods.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:39.903
That's what I was doing.

00:01:39.903 --> 00:01:40.920
All right, here we go.

00:01:41.925 --> 00:01:44.258
- [Maitreyi] Spin the wheel.

00:01:45.425 --> 00:01:46.710
- Okay.
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.530
- Passed gas and- (laughs)

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.010
- If you're saying you haven't,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.490
that's such a lie.
- You're a liar.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.100
- Why do you think I own a dog?

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.850
Like, that's really-
- That's my dog.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:55.830
I've totally blamed my dog.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.217
- It's Melody. Melody,
why'd you fart, bro?

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.520
- You know, granted that
was when I was younger.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.320
Like now, I'll just be like, "My bad."

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.310
Like, I'll just-

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.320
- That's called accountability.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.153
That's why we love you.

00:02:04.153 --> 00:02:05.640
- That's accountability and age.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.010
I think if we've aged,
you just don't care.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:08.843
Yeah.

00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:09.676
- That's fair.

00:02:09.676 --> 00:02:10.740
- It just, it leaves.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.460
But I have blamed my dog before.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.710
Okay. Here's another one.

00:02:16.765 --> 00:02:17.598
Here we go.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.094
- [Maitreyi] Yes.

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:21.710
- Never have I ever sang
to my stuffed animals?

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.080
- Yeah.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:23.913
I have.

00:02:23.913 --> 00:02:25.210
- You have?
- Have you not?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.043
- You know what?

00:02:26.043 --> 00:02:27.493
- Was that not a universal experience?

00:02:27.493 --> 00:02:28.840
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.673
No?

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.980
- Specifically, stuffed animals?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:33.930
No.
- Really?

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.070
- But to like dolls...

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.380
Like, I don't know if I did stuffed-

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.840
Yo, Care Bears. Yes, I did.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.040
- I love Care Bears.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.130
- I love Care- I love Sunshine.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.620
- I would line up my stuffed
animals like along my bed.

